note Control for unroll-growth.om with unroll removed: the same body is valid OM-2 and runs; exit
note status oracle/s3s4 (python3): grow 5 mod 256. Shows the refusal is the word bound, not the body.
note Contract section 4 lines 109-111: a function's emitted words after unrolling are at most 65536,
note else error 14 (obligation=growth). Two nested unroll 64 loops make 4096 copies of a 12-statement
note body of unsigned ops on run-time values (each statement at least two instructions, so at least
note 98304 words). Each loop alone is within the 64-copy bound; the word bound refuses it.
note Twin unroll-growth-diag.om checks the om2 diag record.
om2
fn grow a ulong to ulong
x = a
s = add a 1
t = add a 2
u = add a 3
for i ulong 64
for j ulong 64
x = add mul x 3 add s add i j
s = xor s shr x 7
t = add t mul s x
u = xor u shl t 3
x = add x mul u 5
s = add s xor x t
t = xor t shr s 11
u = add u mul t 9
x = xor x add u s
s = mul s add x 1
t = add t xor u 13
u = xor u add s t
end
end
ret xor xor x s xor t u
end
fn main to int
ret int and grow 5 255
end
